## The Dashboard panels of myx.distro-remote, declared once (F12.2 of the refactorings epic): a panel a line,
## TAB-separated, read as plain text by `--manager-dashboard-read` (LocalTools.ManagerDashboard.include), so what
## this console offers is known with no python.
##   panel  <group>  <name>  <label>  <reader>  <include>  <read>
##       a panel of a group, `root` being the Dashboard itself: its reader is a function of <include>, a file under
##       myx/ (`-` where the reader is `.local`'s own); <read> is `named` where the panel is printed only when it is
##       asked for by its name, `-` otherwise.
## No panel on day one: the remote console registers none of `.local`'s Machine and Disk Space (F11.4), and its own
## panels are a later feature, named when wanted. Its Dashboard is empty until then.
